# Authenticated Windows 2000 SP4 kernel/HAL export baselines.
#
# The PE import descriptor always names NTOSKRNL.EXE or HAL.DLL, but Setup
# selects one of several source binaries for those loaded modules. The import
# gate must resolve against every source image an in-scope target can run:
# NTKRNLMP for the Phase 2d SMP VM, and the ACPI HALs for real hardware, not
# only the Standard-PC/MPS images used by the current VMs.
#
# Source: D:\isos\win2ksp4-retail.ISO, I386\, measured.
#
# **Eight** HAL images, not seven. HALBORG.DLL was missed on the first pass
# because it is the one kernel HAL the media ships *uncompressed*, so it does
# not match the HAL*.DL_ pattern the others were enumerated by - the same
# enumeration gap this manifest exists to close. It is a real kernel HAL
# (export section "HAL.dll", 98 names including HalInitSystem and
# KeGetCurrentIrql, FileDescription "Hardware Abstraction Layer DLL") for the
# SGI Visual Workstation 320/540, a machine no target of this project will ever
# be. It is listed anyway, because a completeness claim that rests on an argued
# exception is the thing that just went wrong. If a future required symbol ever
# turns out to be missing from halborg.dll alone, delete this row and say so
# here - narrowing the claim deliberately is fine; discovering it by accident is
# not.
#
# Format:
#   PACKED OUTPUT PROVIDER VERSION LENGTH SHA256
#
# PACKED names ending in "_" are cabinet-compressed and expanded with
# expand.exe; a name that does not is copied verbatim off the media.

